Fictional EP Tracklist

Track 1: Jar 18 Keeps Moving After the Hand Stops
- Story & Context: The debut opens at 104 BPM with Nadège using a loose-seed kayamb whose internal grains continue sliding for a fraction of a second after each abrupt hand stop. Luc removes the hi-hat entirely and programs only kick, rim, and one two-note pulse-wave bass figure. The tiny seed-settling tail becomes the track’s high-frequency subdivision. Joël enters with roulèr on alternate cycles, leaving enough space that the listener can hear the jar-like rattle decay. Anaïs answers every fourth synth phrase with one bent bobre note. At the midpoint, Nadège switches to a denser seed filling without changing the rhythm, making the same gesture sound shorter and more compressed. Rémi holds one prepared-organ suspended fifth across the transition. The final bar ends with every instrument stopping together except the seeds, which continue settling inside the kayamb for one last audible cascade.
